version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2025-05-01"
url: "https://github.com/Bashford-Rogers-lab/SpatioEv"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bashford-Rogers-lab/SpatioEv"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later

keywords:
  - spatial biology
  - multiplexed imaging
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - single-cell analysis
  - tissue microenvironment
  - pancreatic cancer
  - pseudotime
  - ECM

abstract: >-
  SpatioEv is a Python toolbox for reusable spatial analysis over
  multiplexed imaging data, with extensions for spatial transcriptomics
  workflows such as 10x Xenium. It focuses on per-cell spatial features,
  neighborhood organization, cell–cell and cell–ECM interactions, niche
  graph summaries, and trajectory-ready feature engineering. Key
  capabilities include Ripley and Moran spatial statistics families,
  DBSCAN-based niche boundary detection, cell proximity graphs, ECM–cell
  bipartite graphs, invasion scoring, and pseudotime branch analysis.
